diff --git a/research/integration/stream_readiness_b8n5_v1/GITHUB_ISSUE_DRAFT.md b/research/integration/stream_readiness_b8n5_v1/GITHUB_ISSUE_DRAFT.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5182c26
--- /dev/null
+++ b/research/integration/stream_readiness_b8n5_v1/GITHUB_ISSUE_DRAFT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,169 @@
+# Proposed successor #4390/#3876: distinguish descriptor readiness from buffered complete frames
+
+UNPOSTED draft; retrospective delivery of local b8n5, not public preregistration.
+Do not modify #4390 or any predecessor allocation. This is a new multiple-frame
+I/O-composition question after r9k4's one-terminal-frame result.
+
+# Stream readiness versus buffered frame availability — b8n5
+
+Allocation: `stream-readiness-b8n5-20260926-01`. **Local preregistration only**.
+New scientific question after closed #4231 and the original r9k4 study, now
+separately owned for delivery by #4390. Related notification integration #3876
+and result/recovery #2789. Preserve every old source/result and foreign branch.
+Intake main: `4c701cc51b06296268ad8d9ae3eff1dd6f2d379d`.
+Proposed additive path: `research/integration/stream_readiness_b8n5_v1/**`.
+Proposed branch: `research/stream-readiness-20260926-b8n5`; not remotely created.
+
+## H
+A selector guarding a blocking buffered readline does not implement a bounded
+complete-message receive contract. (1) Read-ahead can place additional complete
+frames in a user buffer while the kernel descriptor is not readable. (2) A
+readable descriptor can contain only a prefix; readline can wait beyond the
+selector's original timeout. A single explicit byte accumulator plus nonblocking
+raw reads should preserve frame order and observed-deadline classification,
+return partial state within the authored budget plus measured scheduling slack,
+and support subsequent **diagnostic read-only collection** without any data replay.
+This is a known I/O composition boundary, not a Python defect, a deployed-runtime
+vulnerability or a novel framing algorithm.
+
+## T
+Two collectors over identical authored cooperative byte streams:
+- FD_THEN_BUFFERED: actual select.select(fd) then io.BufferedReader.readline.
+- EXPLICIT_BUFFER: inspect own bytearray first, otherwise select and nonblocking
+  os.read; retain prefixes; decode UTF-8/JSON only after LF.
+
+Eight conditions: SINGLE, COALESCED_TWO, COALESCED_THREE, SEPARATE_TWO,
+SPLIT_EARLY, SPLIT_LATE, TRUNCATED_EOF, SILENT_OPEN.
+First bytes are written before the clock origin and acknowledged out-of-band.
+The reader is fully initialized before this origin. Second chunks arrive at
+60 ms (separate/early) or340 ms (late); late and early splits bisect a UTF-8
+code point. Writer closes at420 ms except truncated EOF at80 ms. No unframed
+prefix is accepted. A single writer and reader with no competing consumers.
+
+Local pilot:8 conditions x2 collectors x3 fresh repetitions=48 cases/96 separately
+executed actors. Three immutable16-case batches, one per container invocation,
+alternating collector order. Budget200 ms; candidate return tolerance50 ms.
+Each actor await<=4 s, outer batch supervisor25 s, outer tool35 s. Stop after an
+incomplete batch, without retry/replacement/exclusion/pooling/source tuning.
+
+No GUI, task input, model/provider, experimental network, package installation or
+user data. Linux anonymous pipe, same-host monotonic clock. Standard-library-only
+CPython. No Docker/OrbStack image attestation. OS clock and CPU frequency are not
+calibrated; no hard-real-time or whole-product latency claim.
+
+Construction:one separately identified16-case development batch;12 pure unit
+methods;15 effective prefreeze copied-evidence controls, excluding source check
+until FREEZE exists. Development outputs stay excluded. All succeeded; no
+scientific actor was rerun. One redundant same-file audit read was removed before
+freeze; it does not change collector semantics or the table. Record the original
+development audit and the re-audit separately.
+
+## D — fixed full table
+Per repetition, require:
+
+| Scenario | FD_THEN_BUFFERED | EXPLICIT_BUFFER |
+|---|---|---|
+| SINGLE | COMPLETE,1 timely | COMPLETE,1 timely |
+| COALESCED_TWO | BUDGET_EXHAUSTED,1 timely | COMPLETE,2 timely |
+| COALESCED_THREE | BUDGET_EXHAUSTED,1 timely | COMPLETE,3 timely |
+| SEPARATE_TWO | COMPLETE,2 timely | COMPLETE,2 timely |
+| SPLIT_EARLY | COMPLETE,1 timely | COMPLETE,1 timely |
+| SPLIT_LATE | COMPLETE_LATE,0 timely | BUDGET_EXHAUSTED,0 timely |
+| TRUNCATED_EOF | EOF_INCOMPLETE,0 timely | EOF_INCOMPLETE,0 timely |
+| SILENT_OPEN | BUDGET_EXHAUSTED,0 timely | BUDGET_EXHAUSTED,0 timely |
+
+PASS_LOCAL_BUFFERED_READINESS_BOUNDARY additionally requires all48 complete,
+source/process/read/write bytes and frame identities reconcile; all candidate
+returns occur by250 ms; split-late baseline returns no earlier than340 ms;
+coalesced baseline has read all written bytes before its failed readiness wait,
+and its later diagnostic extraction obtains the remaining complete frames before
+writer close without any new raw read. Tail writes must begin no earlier than
+the declared offset and finish within50 ms of it. Every final received byte equals
+the exact emitted stream; final EOF is observed. Truncated prefixes remain partial
+and silent-open timeout is not EOF. No authority or retry permission. All96 actor
+and3 outer exits0; separate raw audit no errors;16 effective well-formed controls
+all reject with no no-op or parser exception.
+
+Complete contradictory data => FAIL at the named boundary. Timing discrimination
+not exposed, missing source/process/raw bytes, timeout or audit failure => HOLD/STOP.
+No gate is loosened after first pilot output. A deliberately incomplete comparator
+failure is not retrospectively alleged to be a current production failure.
+
+## C
+Real io.BufferedReader supplies buffering; a transparent RawIOBase.readinto wrapper
+logs actual os.read below it. A pure unit compares its output to FileIO. Instrumentation
+can change overhead; no uninstrumented speed claim is made. Fixed writes smaller than
+PIPE_BUF and a readiness barrier guarantee this directed coalescence; natural
+coalescence frequency is unmeasured. BufferedReader and select are valid separately.
+Postparse deadline validation is shared by both arms: even the blocking comparator
+never labels its late line as timely. The diagnostic drain intentionally bypasses
+that comparator's readiness gate and is NOT part of its budgeted success.
+
+## U
+No arbitrary concurrent-writer framing, authentication, shared-reader streams,
+current native transport adoption, model consumption, task effects, latency/token
+savings, natural failure probabilities, cross-platform support or hard deadline.
+A successful parse proves neither observation freshness nor action authority.
+Combined calibrated measurement uncertainty u_c and coverage factor k are not
+estimated; the50 ms bound is a preregistered engineering gate, not an uncertainty
+interval. Three technical repetitions are reported as medians/ranges only.
+
+## Variable and unit table
+
+| Symbol/name | Meaning | SI unit | Definition | Domain/assumption | Type |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| fd | 私有パイプの読取記述子 | 1 | 単一readerが所有するOS記述子 | 非負整数、同一パイプ寿命 | integer scalar |
+| t0 | 共通計測開始時刻 | s (stored ns) | 両actor READY後の親monotonic標本 | 同一host時計 | integer scalar |
+| d | 収集期限 | s (stored ns) | t0から200 ms後 | t0と同一時計 | integer scalar |
+| t_return | 収集処理の戻り時刻 | s (stored ns) | collect終了の実monotonic標本 | 診断読取より前 | integer scalar |
+| t_checked | 完全フレームの検証終了時刻 | s (stored ns) | decode/identity検査直後の標本 | raw読取後 | integer scalar |
+| B | まだ消費していないbytes | 1 (bytes count is a data unit) | reader所有bytearray | 順序を保存、同時変更なし | byte vector |
+| R | raw読取の累積bytes | 1 | os.readで得たbytesを順番に連結 | 単一reader | byte vector |
+| F | 取り出したフレームbytesの累積 | 1 | 完全LFフレームの順序付き連結 | 再送・重複消費なし | byte vector |
+| n | 要求されたフレーム数 | 1 | SINGLE等1、TWO2、THREE3 | 1..3 | integer scalar |
